# LLM provider egress IPs — used ONLY in `egress-apply.sh --direct` mode.
#
# Why this is the fragile mode: most providers front their API with a CDN or
# anycast, so these addresses rotate without notice and your run dies mid-engagement
# with a TLS timeout that looks like a provider outage.
#
# Preferred: leave this empty and use the default proxy mode, where
# proxy/squid.conf enforces a *domain* allowlist and IP rotation is irrelevant.
#
# If you must pin IPs, resolve them immediately before the run and re-check after:
#   getent ahostsv4 api.deepseek.com | awk '{print $1"/32"}'
#
# api.deepseek.com:
# 203.0.113.0/32
